"assessment_outcome": "temporarily_unfit",
"explanation": "The patient has a verified history of a severe hypoglycaemic event occurring only 2 weeks ago. According to the supplied guideline evidence, a minimum non-driving period of six weeks is generally required after such an event to allow for the re-establishment of glucose control patterns and resolution of impaired hypoglycaemia awareness. Although the patient's current regimen minimises hypoglycaemia and specialist information is available, the established restriction based on the timing of the recent severe event overrides these positive factors. The absence of a blackout does not negate the requirement for the six-week waiting period following a confirmed severe hypoglycaemic event.",
